# skyland.blueprint.pdl - the MASTER PLAN of the Centroid skyland (2026-11-10). One row per fact; rows are `TAG | field | field | ...`.
# SOURCE: the owner's target picture /home/no/Downloads/goal-centroid-skyland.jpeg (a Dynmap screenshot of someone else's Minecraft build; the picture is NOT stored in this repo).
# This file is OUR abstraction: masses, positions, zones, a route. It is not a block-by-block copy and it uses our own names.
# ACCURACY: every coordinate was ESTIMATED by claude from ONE oblique picture (looking from the south-west, perspective foreshortening, no depth). Expect +-3 cells. Nothing here was measured.
# FRAME: x grows east (image right), y grows south (toward the viewer), z grows up in BLOCKS; origin = north-west corner of the grid. One plan cell is cell_blocks x cell_blocks blocks.
# The three big islands overlap on purpose: the lobes are joined, the shoulder is the stepped ramp, the plateau is higher with a cliff above the village lobe.
# ISLAND  | id | kind | cx | cy | rx | ry | top_z | depth | role      (an ellipse in plan; the underside tapers to a point `depth` blocks below top_z)
# ZONE    | id | island | kind | shape | a | b | c | d | note       (shape ell: cx cy rx ry; shape rect: x0 y0 x1 y1)
# WATER   | id | kind | points x:y;x:y;... | width | z | note        (kinds river, pond, fall (over a cliff onto a lower island), voidfall (off an edge into the void))
# BUILD   | id | kind | x0 | y0 | w | d | base_z | wall_h | roof | note   (a footprint box; w along x, d along y)
# WAYPOINT| id | name | x | y | z | island | note                   (0 is the start, 15 is the goal: the tour of the picture)
# ROUTE   | from | to | kind | note                                 (kinds forest-path, path, stairs-up, stairs-down, bridge, plaza)

META | name | skyland master plan (working name: Centroid skyland)
META | status | PLAN. Estimated from one picture. Checked 2026-11-10 by an ad-hoc awk script (see the doc); a proper C op and harness case are the proposal.
META | doc | #.#.calendar-dox/!.HQ-IQ-BOOK/16.game/CENTROID-SKYLAND-BLUEPRINT-2026-11-10.md
SCALE | cell_blocks | 4
GRID | 72 | 52
VOID | z | -80 | below the lowest island nothing exists; waterfalls fall into it

